  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Phosphorus trioxide reacts with water to form phosphorous acid,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>When acetic acid is heated with phosphorus pentachloride, acetyl chloride is obtained. In this reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>COOH</mi></math> group is converted to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mi>COCl</mi></math> group. The side products are phosphorus oxychloride and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>COCl</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>POCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;undergo disproportionation reaction with sodium hydroxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow/></mover><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>NaH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Due to the presence two&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>&nbsp;bonds,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;acts as reducing agent. It reduces&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>&#8595;</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
